# The rest of the tutorial: from the world map after getting up to the closing frame, recorded on its own
# and started from the opening take's checkpoint (its save from arriving on the world map,
# build/rec_opening2/saves/01_get_up.json, copied to the --save-path before the take), so the opening is
# not replayed. Continue loads it; everything after is tutorial.cli's own second half. The take keeps a
# checkpoint at each arrival on the world map (saves/ in its folder), so any later part can be re-shot the
# same way.
#
# FLAGS: as tutorial.cli's (the start-area, observe-only, npc-static, npc-affinity, job-only and
#        force-encounter flags act on the scenes and journeys still to come), plus --save-path.
allow-flag-miss --start-area
allow-flag-miss --observe-only

wait mode MainMenu 900
mark resume
click menu Continue
wait mode WorldView 900
cursor rest
hold 2

# The protagonist screen, the way a player opens it: Escape, then Protagonist.
pause
wait 900
click menu Protagonist
wait 900

mark anatomy
clip anatomy
click tab anatomy
wait 900
cursor rest
hold 6
clip end anatomy

mark memory
clip memory
click tab memory
wait 900
cursor rest
hold 6
clip end memory

# The inventory: the sword in hand, the cloak and clothes, the backpack. Open the backpack and eat
# the bread in it.
mark inventory
clip inventory
click tab inventory
wait 900
cursor rest
hold 5
click element backpack
wait 900
hold 3
click element content:bread
wait 900
cursor rest
hold 4
click element consume
wait 900
hold 3
clip end inventory

# The humors: the bread's humors have entered the paunch at the spiral's mouth (index 0 is the
# newest). Pointing at it shows what it is and what it does to a die.
mark humors
clip humors
click tab humors
wait 900
cursor rest
hold 5
point element humor:paunch:0
hold 6
point element humor:paunch:1
hold 4
cursor rest
hold 3
clip end humors

click back
wait 900
click menu Continue
wait mode WorldView 900

# ── Travel to the farm ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
mark travel_farm
clip travel_farm
travel 7011
wait 900
cursor rest
hold 4
travel-go
wait mode EncounterPrompt 900
clip end travel_farm

# ── The first fight: a wolf on the road ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# --force-encounter puts a wolf on this journey's middle step. The fight is seeded end to end (the
# arena from the run's GameRng, the wolf from the travel generator, every roll from the fight's own
# stream), so its course is the same on every replay whatever the model wrote before it: the wolf
# starts far off and needs two of our turns to close, then falls to the fifth snap thrust. Our own
# turns are ended to let it come; it never lands a blow.
mark fight_1
clip fight_1
cursor rest
hold 4
click engage
wait mode Fighting 900
cursor rest
hold 5
regions
# Let the wolf come: two turns ended, each once it is ours.
wait turn 900
click end-turn
wait turn 900
click end-turn
# A turn of ours, if the fight is still on: wait for our move, thrust, spend humors only while the roll
# falls short, end the turn. (The skipped count covers every command of the block after the guard.)
skip-unless fighting 21
wait turn 900
click skill Short Sword
click skill Snap Thrust
click fighter enemy
cursor rest
hold 3
dice
click humor hepar needed
click die needed
click humor spleen needed
click die needed
click humor pulmones needed
click die needed
click humor paunch needed
click die needed
hold 2
click continue
cursor rest
hold 2
click end-turn
wait 900

# A turn of ours, if the fight is still on: wait for our move, thrust, spend humors only while the roll
# falls short, end the turn. (The skipped count covers every command of the block after the guard.)
